    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
    <tr>
        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <h1><a name="UserStory"></a><b>User Story</b></h1>

<p><b>Background/Business Context</b></p>

<p>Currently products and product reference data (Line Of Business, Class Of Business, ASLOB, etc.) is housed, created and maintained in custom object records (tables) in D365 Dataverse. These values are then used in Product Maps (or Mappings) which are in turn related to a specific member account and related contracts, which are then consumed by other systems such as forecasting and operations.</p>

<p><b>As a Data Governance user or System Administrator</b><br/>
I want Salesforce to function as the the System Of Record for creating and updating product data reference table values in RDM, and additionally to have the relevant product fields and field values related to the entries on any Draft and Active Product Maps that are imported and/or created in Salesforce</p>

<p>So that we can:</p>

<ol>
	<li>More easily manage the product reference data in a manner similar to our current process but with improved features such as duplicate prevention, approval processes, automated notifications, product rules, and date-driven lifecycle management both in the reference table entries and as related to contracts.</li>
	<li>Be in a better position to start/stop the sale/use of a specifc product entry within a matter of hours instead of days or weeks.</li>
	<li>Better support the future functionality of creating and managing contracts, approvals, etc. directly in Salesforce.</li>
	<li>Potentially eliminate the need for RDM in the future.</li>
</ol>


<hr />

<h1><a name="Background%2FBusinessContext"></a><b>Background / Business Context</b></h1>

<p>This framework ensures:</p>

<ul>
	<li><b>One-to-one name/code mapping between Salesforce and RDM</b></li>
	<li><b>Governance control over product data</b></li>
	<li><b>Controlled creation and deactivation</b></li>
	<li><b>Prevention of duplicate values</b></li>
	<li><b>Clear auditability and lifecycle management</b></li>
</ul>


<hr />

<h1><a name="ScopeofThisStory"></a><b>Scope of This Story</b></h1>

<p>This story covers:</p>

<ul>
	<li>Creation of Salesforce custom objects (one per spreadsheet provided)</li>
	<li>Creation of fields (all spreadsheet columns as free text fields)</li>
	<li><del>Date-driven Active/Inactive management via</del> <b><del>Valid From</del></b> <del>and</del> <b><del>Valid To</del></b> <del>(manual Status picklist removed)</del></li>
	<li><del>Duplicate prevention</del></li>
	<li>Access control and governance</li>
	<li>High-level reference to RDM sync requirement (integration design out of scope)</li>
</ul>


<hr />

<h1><a name="OutofScope"></a><b>Out of Scope</b></h1>

<ul>
	<li>MuleSoft integration design or implementation</li>
	<li>RDM technical synchronization logic</li>
	<li>Deletion confirmation workflow with RDM</li>
	<li>Downstream object relationship modeling (TBD)</li>
	<li>Hierarchical relationships between product entities (future phase)</li>
</ul>


<hr />

<h1><a name="ObjectstoBeCreated"></a><b>Objects to Be Created</b></h1>

<p>Each spreadsheet provided will become its own <b>Salesforce Custom Object</b> (final naming convention TBD):</p>

<ul>
	<li><del>Products</del> - covered in <a href="https://accelins.atlassian.net/browse/SF-1015" title="smart-link" class="external-link" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://accelins.atlassian.net/browse/SF-1015</a></li>
	<li>Sub Products</li>
	<li>POG Products</li>
	<li>OSFI Codes</li>
	<li>Member Products – Programs</li>
	<li>Lines of Business</li>
	<li>Classes of Business</li>
	<li>ASLOBS</li>
	<li>BEEGAP</li>
	<li>Solvency II</li>
</ul>




<hr />

<h1><a name="FieldRequirements"></a><b>Field Requirements</b></h1>

<h2><a name="FieldsfromSpreadsheet"></a><b>Fields from Spreadsheet</b></h2>

<p><del>Every column in the corresponding spreadsheet must be created as a custom field.</del></p>

<p><del>All fields must be:</del></p>

<ul>
	<li><del>Free text</del></li>
	<li><del>No enforced length restriction</del></li>
	<li><del>Not required (unless required for uniqueness logic)</del></li>
</ul>


<hr />

<h2><a name="RecordNameField"></a><b>Record Name Field</b></h2>

<p><del>The</del> <b><del>Name</del></b> <del>field must:</del></p>

<ul>
	<li><del>Be required</del></li>
	<li><del>Be unique within the object</del></li>
	<li><del>Be used for strict name/code matching with RDM</del></li>
</ul>


<p><del>Duplicate values must:</del></p>

<ul>
	<li><del>Be prevented via validation rule or unique constraint</del></li>
	<li><del>Block save action</del></li>
	<li><del>Prevent record progression</del></li>
</ul>


<hr />

<h1><a name="LifecycleDateFields"></a><b>Lifecycle Date Fields</b></h1>

<p><del>Each object must include:</del></p>

<ul>
	<li><b><del>Valid From (Date)</del></b> <del>– required</del></li>
	<li><b><del>Valid To (Date)</del></b> <del>– optional (blank = indefinite/open-ended)</del></li>
</ul>


<hr />

<h2><a name="LifecycleBehaviorandGovernance"></a><b>Lifecycle Behavior and Governance</b></h2>

<p><b><del>Valid From and Valid To fully determine Active/Inactive status.</del></b><br/>
<del>The manual Status picklist is removed and must not be used.</del></p>

<h3><a name="ArecordisActiveifandonlyif%3A"></a><del>A record is</del> <b><del>Active</del></b> <del>if and only if:</del></h3>

<ul>
	<li><del>Valid From is on or before today</del><br/>
<del>AND</del></li>
	<li><del>(Valid To is blank OR Valid To is on or after today)</del></li>
</ul>


<h3><a name="ArecordisInactiveotherwise."></a><del>A record is</del> <b><del>Inactive</del></b> <del>otherwise.</del></h3>

<p><del>Examples:</del></p>

<ul>
	<li><del>Valid From in the future → Inactive</del></li>
	<li><del>Valid To before today → Inactive</del></li>
</ul>


<p><del>Additional rules:</del></p>

<ul>
	<li><del>Future-dated Valid From values are allowed</del></li>
	<li><del>To deactivate, Data Governance sets Valid To to today or a past date</del></li>
	<li><del>Valid From defaults to today</del></li>
	<li><del>Valid To defaults to blank</del></li>
</ul>


<hr />

<h1><a name="StandardValidations"></a><b>Standard Validations</b></h1>

<p><del>The following validations apply on create and edit:</del></p>

<ul>
	<li><del>Valid From is required</del></li>
	<li><del>If Valid To is provided, it must be ≥ Valid From</del></li>
	<li><del>On create, Valid To must not be in the past</del></li>
	<li><del>On edit, Valid To may be set to today or a past date (for deactivation)</del></li>
	<li><del>Name is required and must be unique</del></li>
	<li><del>Prevent conflicting lifecycle logic (Valid From later than Valid To)</del></li>
	<li><del>All validation logic must be enforced at system level</del></li>
</ul>


<hr />

<h1><a name="AccessandGovernanceModel"></a><b>Access and Governance Model</b></h1>

<p>This entire product data reference framework must be <b>restricted</b>.</p>

<hr />

<h2><a name="DataGovernanceRoleCapabilities"></a><b>Data Governance Role Capabilities</b></h2>

<p>Data Governance users can:</p>

<ul>
	<li>Create new records</li>
	<li>Edit existing records</li>
	<li>Deactivate records (set Valid To)</li>
</ul>


<p>They may not:</p>

<ul>
	<li>Create new custom objects</li>
</ul>


<p>Deletion:</p>

<ul>
	<li>Not part of normal lifecycle</li>
	<li>Must be exceptional and documented</li>
</ul>


<hr />

<h2><a name="SystemAdministrator"></a><b>System Administrator</b></h2>

<p>System Administrators retain:</p>

<ul>
	<li>Full system-level access</li>
</ul>


<p>Any deletion must be:</p>

<ul>
	<li>Documented</li>
	<li>Synchronized with RDM</li>
</ul>


<hr />

<h2><a name="ReadOnlyAccess"></a><b>Read-Only Access</b></h2>

<p>All other users:</p>

<ul>
	<li>Can view all records (Active and Inactive)</li>
	<li>Cannot create, edit, deactivate, or delete</li>
</ul>


<hr />

<h1><a name="AuditabilityandReporting"></a><b>Auditability and Reporting</b></h1>

<ul>
	<li>All create, edit, and deactivate actions must be tracked</li>
	<li>Field history tracking required for:
	<ul>
		<li>Name</li>
		<li>Valid From</li>
		<li>Valid To</li>
		<li>Relevant governance fields</li>
	</ul>
	</li>
	<li>All records (Active and Inactive) must be visible</li>
	<li>The system must clearly indicate Active vs Inactive status based on date logic</li>
</ul>


<hr />

<h1><a name="DataIntegrityRules"></a><b>Data Integrity Rules</b></h1>

<ul>
	<li><del>Name must be unique per object</del></li>
	<li><del>Duplicate prevention enforced at system level</del></li>
	<li><del>Valid From required</del></li>
	<li><del>Valid To optional (blank = indefinite)</del></li>
	<li><del>Active/Inactive status driven solely by date logic</del></li>
	<li><del>Deactivation via Valid To (deletion not standard lifecycle)</del></li>
</ul>


<hr />

<h1><a name="CanonicalMappingStatement%28ReferenceOnly%29"></a><b><del>Canonical Mapping Statement (Reference Only)</del></b></h1>

<p><del>Salesforce will serve as the</del> <b><del>canonical mapping authority</del></b> <del>for product reference data.</del></p>

<p><del>All record changes (create, edit, deactivate, delete in exceptional cases) must also occur in RDM via MuleSoft integration.</del></p>

<p><del>Technical integration details are</del> <b><del>out of scope</del></b><del>.</del></p>

<hr />

<h1><a name="AcceptanceCriteria"></a><b>Acceptance Criteria</b></h1>

<hr />

<h2><a name="ObjectCreation"></a><b>Object Creation</b></h2>

<p><b>Given</b> the Salesforce configuration is deployed<br/>
<b>When</b> the framework is reviewed<br/>
<b>Then</b> all required custom objects are present</p>

<hr />

<h2><a name="SpreadsheetFieldsCreated"></a><b>Spreadsheet Fields Created</b></h2>

<p><b><del>Given</del></b> <del>each custom object corresponds to a spreadsheet</del><br/>
<b><del>When</del></b> <del>fields are reviewed</del><br/>
<b><del>Then</del></b> <del>every spreadsheet column exists as a free-text field</del></p>

<hr />

<h2><a name="RecordControls%E2%80%93Creation"></a><b>Record Controls – Creation</b></h2>

<ul>
	<li><del>Missing Name → system blocks save</del></li>
	<li><del>Valid To earlier than Valid From → system blocks save</del></li>
	<li><del>Valid To in the past (on create) → system blocks save</del></li>
	<li><del>Duplicate Name → system blocks save</del></li>
</ul>


<hr />

<h2><a name="RecordControls%E2%80%93EditandDeactivation"></a><b>Record Controls – Edit and Deactivation</b></h2>

<ul>
	<li><del>Valid To set to today/past → record becomes Inactive</del></li>
	<li><del>Valid From set to future → record becomes Inactive until date reached</del></li>
	<li><del>Valid To earlier than Valid From → system blocks save</del></li>
</ul>


<hr />

<h2><a name="Security"></a><b>Security</b></h2>

<ul>
	<li>Data Governance role → create, edit, deactivate</li>
	<li>System Administrator → create, edit, deactivate, exceptional delete</li>
	<li>All other users → view only</li>
</ul>


<hr />

<h2><a name="Governance"></a><b>Governance</b></h2>

<ul>
	<li>Deactivation must be recorded in audit history</li>
	<li>RDM synchronization requirement documented</li>
	<li>Exceptional deletions must be documented and synchronized</li>
</ul>


<hr />

<h2><a name="IntegrationOutofScope"></a><b>Integration Out of Scope</b></h2>

<p><b>Given</b> the story is reviewed<br/>
<b>When</b> scope boundaries are assessed<br/>
<b>Then</b> MuleSoft integration and RDM synchronization logic are clearly marked out of scope</p>
            <br/>
        </td>
    </tr>
    </table>

