                            ]
            </font>

        </td></tr>
        <tr id="comment-body-2638761"><td bgcolor="#ffffff">
            <p><a href="https://accelins.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=712020%3A0d055962-1974-4273-b8d7-7a97dd766aa8" class="user-hover" rel="712020:0d055962-1974-4273-b8d7-7a97dd766aa8" data-account-id="712020:0d055962-1974-4273-b8d7-7a97dd766aa8" accountid="712020:0d055962-1974-4273-b8d7-7a97dd766aa8" rel="noreferrer">Ken Reynolds</a> - As per refinement session please include these scenarios and the Dataverse ID into each of the Product ref data tables:</p>

<ol>
	<li>They need to be read only</li>
	<li>Dataverse_ID__c field must be of type Text(36)</li>
	<li>And it must be excluded from all page layouts</li>
	<li>And it must be hidden from all standard user profiles</li>
	<li>And it must be visible and writable via API only to the MuleSoft integration user</li>
	<li>No user can edit</li>
</ol>


<p><b>Scenario 1: Create hidden Dataverse ID field on Account</b><br/>
  Given the Account object<br/>
  When the field "Dataverse_ID__c" is created<br/>
  Then it must be of type Text(36)<br/>
  And labeled "Dataverse ID"<br/>
  And excluded from all page layouts<br/>
  And visible via API to integration users</p>

<p><b>Scenario 2: New Salesforce Account initially has no Dataverse ID</b><br/>
  Given a user creates a new Account in Salesforce<br/>
  When the record is saved<br/>
  Then "Dataverse_ID__c" should be blank</p>





<p><a href="https://accelins.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=712020%3Aecbcec11-f098-4810-8f24-650664eabec1" class="user-hover" rel="712020:ecbcec11-f098-4810-8f24-650664eabec1" data-account-id="712020:ecbcec11-f098-4810-8f24-650664eabec1" accountid="712020:ecbcec11-f098-4810-8f24-650664eabec1" rel="noreferrer">Ahmed Al-Raweshidy</a> FYI, the above needs to go in this story (which will save time and effort manging similar stories)</p>
        </td></tr>
