            <p><a href="https://accelins.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=712020%3Aa12e418b-2c1e-4b88-aea9-b64500f8f8f9" class="user-hover" rel="712020:a12e418b-2c1e-4b88-aea9-b64500f8f8f9" data-account-id="712020:a12e418b-2c1e-4b88-aea9-b64500f8f8f9" accountid="712020:a12e418b-2c1e-4b88-aea9-b64500f8f8f9" rel="noreferrer">Abby Parker</a> <a href="https://accelins.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=712020%3Aecbcec11-f098-4810-8f24-650664eabec1" class="user-hover" rel="712020:ecbcec11-f098-4810-8f24-650664eabec1" data-account-id="712020:ecbcec11-f098-4810-8f24-650664eabec1" accountid="712020:ecbcec11-f098-4810-8f24-650664eabec1" rel="noreferrer">Ahmed Al-Raweshidy</a> <a href="https://accelins.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=712020%3A0d055962-1974-4273-b8d7-7a97dd766aa8" class="user-hover" rel="712020:0d055962-1974-4273-b8d7-7a97dd766aa8" data-account-id="712020:0d055962-1974-4273-b8d7-7a97dd766aa8" accountid="712020:0d055962-1974-4273-b8d7-7a97dd766aa8" rel="noreferrer">Ken Reynolds</a> <a href="https://accelins.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=712020%3Aef6dc51c-ea62-4cfb-9a5c-4c879c9daa7a" class="user-hover" rel="712020:ef6dc51c-ea62-4cfb-9a5c-4c879c9daa7a" data-account-id="712020:ef6dc51c-ea62-4cfb-9a5c-4c879c9daa7a" accountid="712020:ef6dc51c-ea62-4cfb-9a5c-4c879c9daa7a" rel="noreferrer">Alan Slater</a> <a href="https://accelins.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=712020%3A6eb6f4d6-668a-457c-b78b-ae35e825e64f" class="user-hover" rel="712020:6eb6f4d6-668a-457c-b78b-ae35e825e64f" data-account-id="712020:6eb6f4d6-668a-457c-b78b-ae35e825e64f" accountid="712020:6eb6f4d6-668a-457c-b78b-ae35e825e64f" rel="noreferrer">Gabriel Fuoco</a> </p>

<p>Regarding security on the above list of objects, as per our understanding, we are following the steps below:</p>

<ol>
	<li>PSG_DataGovernance_User, for this particular permission set group, we are giving create/read/edit permission for the list of above objects.</li>
	<li>Need more clarification on which permission set groups or profiles should have only read access? Then I can give read-only access to the respective permission set groups or profiles, and the rest of them I will provide no access.</li>
</ol>

        </td></tr>
